---
description: Prevent Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks by properly escaping and sanitizing user input
alwaysApply: true
---

xss-prevention:

- Always escape or sanitize user-generated content before rendering it in HTML
- Use framework-provided escaping mechanisms (React JSX, Vue templates)
- Use trusted sanitization libraries like DOMPurify for rich content
- Implement Content Security Policy (CSP) headers
- Validate input on both client and server side

Dangerous patterns to avoid:
```javascript
element.innerHTML = userInput;
<div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: userComment }} />
<div v-html="userContent"></div>
```

Safe patterns to use:
```javascript
element.textContent = userInput;
<div>{userInput}</div>
const clean = DOMPurify.sanitize(userInput);
```
